{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d9b5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0d127-0511-7921-a79b-fbe9b8416c0a"},"sequence":2869,"recorded_at":1780531400005733,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"2935b83d-2af1-400b-8bec-61864cd8ed2c","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"2935b83d-2af1-400b-8bec-61864cd8ed2c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"2935b83d-2af1-400b-8bec-61864cd8ed2c"},"call_id":"call_01a0d156674970b7887b0c79c4198fe3","text":"Read text file `internal/cloneplan/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# Projection Clause Coverage (TASK-260830-1jmmqn)\n2|\n3|Owner: `internal/cloneplan`. Authority:\n4|`internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`, Section 13.14.2 \"Fidelity,\n5|projection, and lineage\" (line 10548+): the Projection Plan 1.0.0\n6|table, the component schemas that follow it\n7|(ProjectionItemMapping, ProjectionTargetOperation,\n8|ExpectedTargetResource, SynthesizedProjectionEvent,\n9|TransactionPlan, ReadBackPlan, ResumeProjectionPlan,\n10|RollbackPlan, ContractRequirement), and the Clone Projected Object\n11|Manifest 1.0.0 paragraph. Schema URNs come from the Section 1\n12|registry table (lines 168-169). Section 13.14.4 carries no\n13|constraint on these shapes. This is the SECOND leaf's clause record\n14|for the fidelity-projection-and-validation-contracts story; record\n15|clause-to-test bindings here. The `internal/traceability` registry\n16|edit belongs to the Story's final leaf, not this one. Planning\n17|semantics (strategy/profile choice, checkpoint message authority,\n18|inactive tools/instructions, token metadata) belong to the sibling\n19|planning leaf (TASK-260924-3n78rv), not this one.\n20|\n21|## Why this package exists\n22|\n23|Section 13.14.2 states the Projection Plan 1.0.0 closed table, the\n24|nine component records, and the Clone Projected Object Manifest\n25|1.0.0 closed shape with its branch-exact entries. No landed package\n26|owns them: the `canonicaljson` closed-shape registry recognizes\n27|`urn:ax:schema:projection-plan` and\n28|`urn:ax:schema:clone-projected-object-manifest` only to refuse them\n29|(`rejectUnsupportedImmutableObjectShape`, pinned by that table's\n30|census), so this package is the validating owner. The sibling\n31|fidelity leaf owns dispositions, reasons, and the Fidelity Report;\n32|where the plan references sibling contracts (Migration Checkpoint,\n33|Read-Back, Validation Report, Lineage Receipt, Bundle Manifest)\n34|only the identity or digest field is carried.\n35|\n36|## Landed-owner reuse\n37|\n38|| Scope | Owner | Use |\n39||---|---|---|\n40|| Strict JSON framing | `internal/environ` | `DecodeStrictObject` at `decodeStrictObject`: the plan, the manifest, and every nested shape refuse lone-surrogate escapes, duplicate members, non-objects, and trailing data before any member is read |\n41|| Character string measure | `internal/environ` | `StringLength` at every bound, both entries |\n42|| String/uint53/digest/UUID bounds | `internal/environ` | `CheckStringBounds`, `CheckUint53Bounds`, `CheckDigest`, `CheckUUIDv7` at every decode site |\n43|| Sorted-unique arrays | `internal/environ` | `CheckSortedUniqueStrings`, `CheckSortedUniqueDigests` at every decode site |\n44|| SemVer grammar | `internal/environ` | `CheckSemver` behind the contract version gate, both entries |\n45|| Environment Tuples | `internal/sessadapter` | `DecodeTuple` at all three tuple members, both entries |\n46|| Resource Limits | `internal/sessadapter` | `DecodeResourceLimits` at `resource_limits`, both entries |\n47|| Canonical bytes, digests, UUIDs | `internal/canonicaljson`, `internal/scalar` | `Canonicalize`, `SHA256Digest`, `ParseDigest`, `ParseUUIDv7` |\n48|| Closed extension values | `internal/clonebundle` | `CheckExtensionsClosed` at every extension member on decode; `EncodeExtensions` on build |\n49|| Omit-self digest | `internal/clonebundle` | `OmitSelfDigest` behind `verifySelfDigest` |\n50|| Workspace Binding | `internal/clonebundle` | `DecodeWorkspaceBinding` at `target_workspace`, both entries |\n51|| Capture classes (9) | `internal/clonebundle` | `ValidCaptureClass` for `security_exclusions` |\n52|| Dispositions (7), reasons (19+ext) | `internal/clonefidelity` | `ValidDisposition` for `expected_disposition` and policy values; `ValidReasonCode` for mapping reasons |\n53|\n54|No behavior in any reused package changed: this leaf adds a new\n55|package only and edits no landed file (importer grid below).\n56|\n57|## Interpretation record (decided, pinned)\n58|\n59|These readings are taken where the pinned text underdetermines the\n60|gate. Each is pinned by a named test, not prose.\n61|\n62|| # | Reading | Test |\n63||---|---|---|\n64|| I1 | `item_mappings` are sorted unique by source item key: the plan prose binds \"ordered item mappings\", and the key is the only candidate order | `TestRowOrderSweep` (unsorted + duplicate refuse; ordered admits) |\n65|| I2 | `expected_resources` sort key is the (sequence, key) pair, strictly increasing | `TestRowOrderSweep` (sequence regression, key regression, and full duplicate refuse; both admit shapes admit) |\n66|| I3 | `required_dispositions` is the exact request policy: a non-empty map of classes to sorted unique 1..7 dispositions; key closure is the request owner's stated bound, mirrored | `TestRequiredDispositions` |\n67|| I4 | `forbid_reasons` admits literal bounded strings: the table row types them as strings, not reason codes | `TestForbidReasonsAdmitLiteralStrings` (`frobnicate` seals and decodes) |\n68|| I5 | Operation dependencies name existing strictly-lower sequences: an edge to an absent sequence is not a DAG over the plan operations | `TestDAGRefusalLiterals` (dangling), `TestDAGExhaustiveSmall` (oracle) |\n69|| I6 | Expected-resource branch rule is the blob-ID arm only: blob rows carry non-null `expected_blob_id`, directory rows null; mode keeps its nullable type on both branches | `TestResourceNullabilityGrid` (12 cells, 6 admit) |\n70|| I7 | Manifest directory `mode` keeps the nullable uint32[0..4095] type; the branch difference is the member set (7 vs 4) | `TestEntryNullabilityGrid`, `TestEntryDecodeBranchGrid` |\n71|| I8 | Manifest entries reuse the plan scalar types (sequence uint53>0, key string[1..512]) because entries partition plan resources | `TestEntryStringEdges`, `TestNumberModel` |\n72|| I9 | `ContractRequirement` carries no extensions member: the pinned text states exactly contract_id and version | `TestContractNoExtensions` |\n73|| I10 | Mapping rows carry no disposition/reason/canonical coupling: the pinned mapping text states none (unlike the fidelity row) | `TestNoDispositionCouplingOnMappings` (12 admit cells) |\n74|| I11 | `total_bytes` admits any uint53: the pinned text states no derivation rule | `TestTotalBytesIsAStatedBoundUntilSpecDefinesDerivation` |\n75|| I12 | Synthesized array position IS the insertion sequence: no order gate is expressible without a sequence member | stated bound below |\n76|| I13 | `canonical_event_ids` are ordered unique (session order), not sorted: descending digests admit, duplicates refuse | `TestSortedUniqueSweep` (canonical-ordered-not-sorted) |\n77|\n78|## Clause map\n79|\n80|| Pinned clause | Production entry | Test |\n81||---|---|---|\n82|| 13.14.2 four plan strategies admitted exactly; archive_only refused | `ValidPlanStrategy`, `BuildProjectionPlan`, `DecodeProjectionPlan` | `TestPlanStrategyOracle` (4 admit + predicate/build/decode; 10 refusals incl. archive_only) |\n83|| 13.14.2 four plan profiles admitted exactly; archive_only refused | `ValidPlanProfile`, both plan entries | `TestPlanProfileOracle` (4 admit; 9 refusals incl. archive_only) |\n84|| 13.14.2 four operation actions admitted exactly | `ValidOperationAction`, both plan entries | `TestOperationActionOracle` (4 admit; 9 refusals) |\n85|| 13.14.2 three synthesized purposes admitted exactly | `ValidSynthesizedPurpose`, both plan entries | `TestSynthesizedPurposeOracle` (3 admit; 8 refusals) |\n86|| 13.14.2 two resource kinds admitted exactly, both shapes | `ValidResourceKind`, all four entries | `TestResourceKindOracle` (2 admit; 7 refusals x 2 shapes x 2 entries) |\n87|| 13.14.2 seven expected dispositions admitted exactly | `clonefidelity.ValidDisposition` via both plan entries | `TestExpectedDispositionOracle` (7 admit; 7 refusals x 2 entries) |\n88|| 13.14.2 mapping reasons are core + reverse-DNS | `clonefidelity.ValidReasonCode` via both plan entries | `TestMappingReasonVocabulary` (20 admit; 7 refusals x 2 entries) |\n89|| 13.14.2 Projection Plan exact 36-member set | `DecodeProjectionPlan` | `TestMemberCensusExactSets`, `TestMemberCensusUnknownMissing`, `TestMemberCensusMiscased`, `TestMemberCensusWrongTypes`, `TestMemberCensusDuplicated`, `TestCensusShapeInventory` |\n90|| 13.14.2 manifest exact 10-member set; blob 7 / directory 4 branch sets | `DecodeProjectedObjectManifest` | same census tests (13 shapes: 36/10/6/5/6/4/4/5/4/4/2/7/4) |\n91|| 13.14.2 schema/version literals | both decode entries | `TestSchemaLiterals` (plan 4+4, manifest 3+1 refusal literals) |\n92|| 13.14.2 `projection_plan_id` is the JCS digest omitting only itself | `BuildProjectionPlan`, `verifySelfDigest` | `TestPlanIdentityIndependent` (test-side JCS recompute agrees; omitting strategy disagrees; tampered claim and non-digest refuse) |\n93|| 13.14.2 `projected_object_manifest_id` under the omission rule | `BuildProjectedObjectManifest`, `verifySelfDigest` | `TestManifestIdentityIndependent` (same shape) |\n94|| 13.14.2 dependencies are lower sequences and form a DAG | `checkOperationOrder`, `checkOperationDAG` (both entries) | `TestDAGExhaustiveSmall` (all 2+16+512 graphs vs oracle, both entries), `TestDAGValidEnumeration` (64+1024 valid DAGs admit), `TestDAGRefusalLiterals` (higher/self/dangling/dup/unordered/decode/cycle), `TestDAGNonContiguousValid` |\n95|| 13.14.2 blob/directory nullability branch-exact (resources) | `checkResourceBranch` (both entries) | `TestResourceNullabilityGrid` (12 cells vs oracle, both entries), `TestResourceBranchLiterals` |\n96|| 13.14.2 blob/directory branch-exact entries | `checkEntryBranch` (build), kind dispatch (decode) | `TestEntryNullabilityGrid` (12 cells), `TestEntryDecodeBranchGrid` (per-member missing/present + mode admission), `TestEntryBranchLiterals` |\n97|| 13.14.2 every sorted-unique array refuses unsorted/duplicated | both entries | `TestSortedUniqueSweep` (8 arrays x 2 shapes x 2 entries + ordered-not-sorted admission) |\n98|| 13.14.2 cross-row order (mappings/resources/entries/contracts) | shared order gates (both entries) | `TestRowOrderSweep` (build violations + decode documents per gate) |\n99|| 13.14.2 string bounds at edge/edge+1, character measure | both entries via `environ.StringLength` | `TestStringBoundsEdges` (5 members x edges x 2 entries), `TestMultibyteMeasure` (512/513 `é`), `TestManifestStringEdges`, `TestEntryStringEdges` |\n100|| 13.14.2 cardinality bounds at edge/edge+1 | factored count gates + both entries | `TestCountEdges` (entry reachability + 64/65 + 129 + 65536/65537) + `TestFactoredCountGates` (6 gates x min/max/min-1/max+1) |\n101|| 13.14.2 Transaction/ReadBack/Resume/Rollback constants refused on any other value | build + decode per component | `TestPlanConstants` (every member incl. near-miss X2 values, every modes shape, every flag, bounded both booleans + 5 non-boolean refusals) |\n102|| 13.14.2 ContractRequirement (contract_id, SemVer; no extensions) | build + decode | `TestContractSemver` (5 admit + 7 refusals x 2 entries), `TestContractNoExtensions` |\n103|| 13.14.2 required_dispositions exact policy from request | build + decode policy gates | `TestRequiredDispositions` (empty + 5 bad shapes x 2 entries + full 7-set admission) |\n104|| 13.14.2 security_exclusions sorted unique capture-class[0..9] | build + decode | `TestSecurityExclusions` (9 admit, 10-count, vocab refusal x 2 entries) + `TestSortedUniqueSweep` |\n105|| 13.14.2 scalar gates (digests, UUIDv7, tuples, workspace, limits) | both entries via landed owners | `TestScalarGates` (14 decode + 11 build rows), `TestManifestScalarGates` (3+3 rows) |\n106|| 13.14.2 AX number model (no fractions/exponents/strings/≥2^53) | decode via `environ.CheckUint53Bounds`; build overflow checks | `TestNumberModel` (6 members x 6 bad values + max admit + 6 build overflows) |\n107|| 13.14.2 closed extensions (reverse-DNS keys, AX values, no nested dup) | both entries via `clonebundle` owner | `TestExtensionsClosed` (admission + build/decode rows + nested dup) |\n108|| 13.14.2 strict framing (dup/trailing/non-object/surrogate/UTF-8) | `decodeStrictObject` | `TestFraming` (9 plan + 3 manifest + 1 surrogate rows) |\n109|| 13.14.2 build UTF-8 pre-marshal gate (every string-valued member refuses invalid UTF-8; decode refuses at the delegated strict frame before dispatch) | build string admissions; decode via `decodeStrictObject` | `TestUTF8RefusalReflectionGrid` (72 reflection-derived members x 5 invalid-UTF-8 classes x both entries) + `TestRegistryPredicatesRefuseInvalidUTF8` (5 predicates x 5 classes) |\n110|| 13.14.2 build-side member census (every input member zeroed) | both build entries | `TestBuildZeroValueCensus` (33 plan cells, 6 admit), `TestBuildZeroValueRows` (mapping/operation/resource/event/contract), `TestBuildZeroValueManifest` (top/entry) |\n111|| 13.14.2 determinism (identical inputs, identical bytes) | both build entries | `TestDeterminism` (10 builds byte-identical per entry) |\n112|| 13.14.2 purity (no durable write) | all four entries | `TestEntriesArePure` (decode never mutates input; every build output decodes clean) |\n113|\n114|## Durability\n115|\n116|This package holds no local state and performs no durable write:\n117|sealing is pure bytes (`json.Marshal` + JCS + SHA-256 over memory),\n118|so crash semantics are vacuous. The durability proof is\n119|determinism plus purity: `TestDeterminism` (ten builds\n120|byte-identical per entry) and `TestEntriesArePure` (decode never\n121|mutates its input; every build output decodes clean).\n122|\n123|## Mutants\n124|\n125|`testdata/mutant_harness.py` ships 117 narrowing rows plus the\n126|harmless `C-doc-comment` SURVIVED control. Every narrowing weakens\n127|one gate to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject,\n128|and every killer drives a production entry alone. Shared gates (one\n129|implementation, two call sites: the vocabulary predicates, the\n130|strict frame, the member census helpers, the order helpers, the\n131|DAG gate, the branch gates, the factored count gates, the modes\n132|constant, the build UTF-8 helpers) carry one plant each with a\n133|killer that drives the production entries; rules implemented twice\n134|(build + decode) carry one plant per side. `N-strategy-route` and\n135|`N-action-route` are the token-preserving attacks: the\n136|searched-for token still matches while the decision changes, and\n137|the killers execute the behavioral oracle suites through both\n138|entries. Single-member-class rows label gates whose reject class\n139|holds exactly one member. The battery runs twice with one raw log\n140|per plant per run carrying the subprocess exit.\n141|\n142|## Importer outcome grid\n143|\n144|This leaf adds `internal/cloneplan` (new files only) and edits no\n145|landed file, so no existing package changes behavior. The grid is\n146|keyed (package, entry, input) over every touched package:\n147|\n148|| Package | Entries | Base | Candidate | Moved classes |\n149||---|---|---|---|---|\n150|| `internal/cloneplan` | 4 entries + 5 predicates (new) | n/a (package absent) | green suite | none (new surface, no importer yet) |\n151|| `internal/environ` | reused gates (untouched) | green | green | none |\n152|| `internal/scalar` | reused scalars (untouched) | green | green | none |\n153|| `internal/canonicaljson` | reused JCS (untouched; registry rows kept) | green | green | none |\n154|| `internal/clonebundle` | reused owners (untouched) | green | green | none |\n155|| `internal/clonefidelity` | reused vocabularies (untouched) | green | green | none |\n156|| `internal/sessadapter` | reused tuple/limits (untouched) | green | green | none |\n157|\n158|## Stated bounds (sibling scope or spec-silent, not waived)\n159|\n160|- `canonical_event_ids` equality with Canonical Session order needs\n161|  the session as an input; only ordered-unique shape is gated here.\n162|- Item-mapping coverage (\"one for every captured/canonical item\")\n163|  needs the manifests as inputs; only the row shape, count, and key\n164|  order are gated here.\n165|- Expected-resource and manifest-entry partitioning against plan\n166|  operations needs the plan as a cross-input; only intra-shape\n167|  rules are gated here.\n168|- Synthesized insertion anchors against canonical IDs need the\n169|  Canonical Session; only digest-or-null shape is gated here.\n170|- `total_bytes` reconciliation is an EXPLICIT STATED BOUND: the\n171|  pinned text states no derivation rule, so any uint53 admits\n172|  (witnessed by\n173|  `TestTotalBytesIsAStatedBoundUntilSpecDefinesDerivation`).\n174|  Owner: spec clarification (agent-session-manager-spec).\n175|- Synthesized array order: array position IS the insertion\n176|  sequence; no order gate is expressible (I12).\n177|- `required_dispositions` key closure is the request owner's bound\n178|  (`sessadapter` checkRequiredDispositions), mirrored exactly (I3).\n179|- `forbid_reasons` admits literal bounded strings (I4), not\n180|  reason-vocabulary members.\n181|- Admission at exactly 1,000,000 mappings is pinned at the factored\n182|  `checkMappingCount` gate plus entry reachability rows, not by\n183|  sealing a million-row plan (see `TestCountEdges` and\n184|  `TestFactoredCountGates`).\n185|- Planning semantics (strategy/profile choice, checkpoint message\n186|  authority, inactive tools/instructions, token metadata) belong to\n187|  the sibling planning leaf (TASK-260924-3n78rv): this leaf gates\n188|  shapes only.\n189|- Sections 13.14.3-13.14.5 and the Read-Back, Validation Report,\n190|  Migration Checkpoint, and Lineage Receipt contracts are sibling\n191|  scope.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
