{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000dbbb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0d127-0511-7921-a79b-fbe9b8416c0a"},"sequence":3128,"recorded_at":1780531400006251,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"2935b83d-2af1-400b-8bec-61864cd8ed2c","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"2935b83d-2af1-400b-8bec-61864cd8ed2c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"2935b83d-2af1-400b-8bec-61864cd8ed2c"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0d157-af8b-7260-b42d-d07f0d81a997"},"task_id":"01a0d157-af8b-7260-b42d-d07f0d81a997","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0d157-af8b-7260-b42d-d07f0d81a997","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 208-211\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-- Admission at exactly 1,000,000 mappings is pinned at the factored\n-  `checkMappingCount` gate plus entry reachability rows, not by\n-  sealing a million-row plan (see `TestCountEdges` and\n-  `TestFactoredCountGates`).\n+- Five-operation DAG coverage is structural, not exhaustive: every\n+  graph through four operations is enumerated against the oracle,\n+  and at five operations every edge class is driven at every\n+  position over the per-edge-local rule pinned by\n+  `TestDAGLocalityStructure` and `TestDAGSingleEdgeLocality`. The\n+  full 33M-graph five-operation enumeration is infeasible and is\n+  not run.\n+- The no-literal-list guard trips on census-scale composites (at\n+  least 10 distinct member names at 40%+ member purity); smaller\n+  literal fragments are below its line by design.\n+- JSON-level member probes (missing/extra/duplicated/wrong-type/\n+  case-variant) run at the decode entries; Go inputs cannot express\n+  an extra, duplicated, or wrong-typed member, so the build-side\n+  member census is the per-field zero-value sweep\n+  (`TestBuildZeroValue*`, reflection-count-checked).\n","final_result":true}}}
